From e77baeb2e81e673e96227a04e63bab73ed381e29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:52:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 083/122] XRECORD: the xdata of earlier versions as R2007+

The xdata strings are UTF-16 since R2007, but the writes were bounded
by the xdata_size of the source: from R2000 the values after the first
strings were cut off, ACadSharp failed on these xrecords ("Arithmetic
operation resulted in an overflow", 8 in sample_AC1015 as R2010).

* src/encode.c (dwg_encode_xdata): Across versions allow up to twice
the size; the size is recalculated afterwards.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/encode.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/encode.c b/src/encode.c
index ca6f8f3..ae8e654 100644
--- a/src/encode.c
+++ b/src/encode.c
@@ -7968,6 +7968,10 @@ dwg_encode_xdata (Bit_Chain *restrict dat, Dwg_Object_XRECORD *restrict _obj,
   if (dat->opts
       & DWG_OPTS_IN) // loosen the overflow checks on dxf/json imports
     end += xdata_size;
+  // the strings are UTF-16 since R2007: up to twice the size, plus the
+  // codepage bytes
+  else if (dat->version != dat->from_version)
+    end += xdata_size + 2 * (size_t)_obj->num_xdata;
 
   while (rbuf)
     {
